Compilation of Henry’s law constants, version 5.0.0 — Rolf Sander (@gc-henry: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gc-sources) { r_4HW63C2ZE42PFRFC294FDPTYWH
Rolf Sander. “Compilation of Henry's law constants (version 5.0.0) for water as solvent.” Atmospheric Chemistry and Physics 23, 10901–12440, 2023. DOI 10.5194/acp-23-10901-2023. [Official article, PDF, supplements, and review history](https://acp.copernicus.org/articles/23/10901/2023/).

Read the definitions, convention/unit conversions, temperature dependence, data-source/evaluation discussion, and one carefully selected species entry with its original references. This very large compilation is a reference for a focused research problem, not an assignment to memorize or ingest every entry. Compare the constant form c/p, its reciprocal, and a dimensionless convention before using any numerical value.

The publisher states CC BY 4.0. Preserve article and underlying source attribution and notices when reusing. This identifies the 2023 version; check the author's linked site for later evaluated editions when needed. Bibliography, publication date, scope, licence, and authorized access checked on 29 October 2026. No article, supplement, or database is copied here.

**Return:** [General chemistry sources — books, courses, data, and research](../Sources.lingua#r_37CHT3QSMD33JDMXE59S6M2ME3).
